371 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 230 0 R
/E (The overarching aim of this project is to architect, develop, and validate an autonomous Service Reliability Engineering \(SRE\) tool that mathematically guarantees the high availability of targeted retail applications.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
372 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 230 0 R
/E (The project moves beyond theoretical cloud concepts by providing a tangible, executable solution tailored for localized edge environments. To achieve this, the project is subdivided into several critical, measurable objectives.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
373 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 230 0 R
/E (Firstly, the project aims to continuously monitor OS-level process tables with a negligible CPU footprint. The monitoring daemon must be invisible to the host system, consuming minimal processing power to ensure it does not cannibalize resources required by the actual POS software.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
374 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 230 0 R
/E (Secondly, the project aims to automatically detect unexpected process terminations and execute recovery sub-processes instantly without human approval. The logic engine must correctly differentiate between a healthy running state and an unexpected closure.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
