378 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 231 0 R
/E (The application is built utilizing a highly efficient, localized technology stack meticulously chosen to ensure cross-platform compatibility, execution speed, and minimal deployment friction.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
379 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 231 0 R
/E (At the core of the infrastructure is Python 3.x. Python was selected due to its robust standard library, its unparalleled ability to interface natively with low- level OS APIs, and its rapid prototyping capabilities.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
380 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 231 0 R
/E (For operating system interfacing, the project relies heavily on the `psutil` and `subprocess` libraries. The `psutil` module is a cross-platform library for retrieving information on running processes and system utilization.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
381 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 231 0 R
/E (Physical hardware emulation, necessary for synthesizing retail transactions and simulating cashier input, is achieved using the `pyautogui` framework. This allows the script to explicitly control the mouse and keyboard.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
