385 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 232 0 R
/E (A defining characteristic of this project is its deliberate avoidance of heavy, expensive, centralized hardware. Because the system is specifically designed to operate on edge devices, localized retail kiosks, and legacy checkout counters, the hardware architecture is intentionally minimalist.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
386 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 232 0 R
/E (It operates on the principle of edge computing, where processing, monitoring, and database storage occur directly at the point of data origin rather than relying on a continuous, high-bandwidth uplink to a centralized cloud server.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
387 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 232 0 R
/E (The application requires a standard x86, x64, or ARM-based processor capable of running a modern desktop operating system \(such as Windows 10/11, macOS, or Linux\).)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
388 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 232 0 R
/E (Crucially, the hardware architecture demands local disk storage for the SQLite database. A standard solid-state drive \(SSD\) is highly preferred to ensure that the rapid, sequential INSERT commands executed during the automated transaction synthesis do not encounter physical disk I/O bottlenecks.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
