/Pg 24 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
420 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 237 0 R
/E (Implementation is strictly centralized within a monolithic `monitor.py` script structure \(which incorporates modular imports for logical separation\).)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
421 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 237 0 R
/E (This monolithic execution approach was deliberately chosen to eliminate dependency latency, prevent module import errors on locked-down retail machines, and ensure the entire SRE infrastructure can be deployed as a single execution point.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
422 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 237 0 R
/E (The implementation is logically phased. The initialization phase handles database generation, executing a synchronous CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS statement to ensure schema safety before any concurrent threads are spawned.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
423 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 237 0 R
/E (The core execution relies on the `psutil.process_iter\(\)` generator instead of instantiating static arrays of all active system processes. This lazy-evaluation approach heavily optimizes memory usage.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
